      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The bias, RMSE and spatial correlation against WOA23 must be computed only on cells where both the model field and WOA23 have data, on one shared grid and one shared mask, and the question's figures depend on that mask choice.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put every field on the WOA23 1° grid, build one mask over all sources with `build_comparison_mask` and apply `.where(mask)` to each before bias, RMSE and pattern correlation, so all three models are scored and ranked on the same cells; report the mask's cell counts (a mask much smaller than the fields means the products disagree about where the ocean is).",
        "`ocean_only=True` (the default) is right here because WOA23 is part of the comparison; take `mean_data` and `mean_reference` from `compute_difference_metrics` over the shared sample and quote them with the bias, not means computed on each source's own cells."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "historical-ssp245-member-continuity",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/historical-ssp245-member-continuity.md",
      "sha256": "02341c56015c6296db14585b4561fc32ca6b4e52e2264bec50eee6746c1d55f6",
      "reason": "The question asks explicitly for a caveat on the ensemble members used in each model's two experiments, and this fragment states that CESM2's ssp245 continues a different member (r10i1p1f1) than the local historical (r1i1p1f1), so historical→ssp245 changes mix forced change with internal variability.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "CESM2 historical is r1i1p1f1 but its ssp245 is r10i1p1f1 (different realisations; historical r10 is not in the archive), so delta SSS and the slope ratio for CESM2 contain forced change plus an inter-member internal-variability difference — state this caveat; GFDL-ESM4 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are r1/r1 and continuous.",
        "Do not fit a trend across the 2014/2015 join (as the separate segments in Fig. 3 already do); each slope is fitted within its own segment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "serial-correlation-and-significance",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/serial-correlation-and-significance.md",
      "sha256": "fe11bd008257a589f44e369faba5fa31ab3cf9ad99280e88c763ac45d2b0e917",
      "reason": "The question requests trend confidence intervals, R-squared, whether the interval excludes zero, and p<0.05 stippling, all of which require an effective sample size because monthly/annual ocean series are strongly autocorrelated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Fit the slopes with `fit_1D_trend`/`fit_trend_map` using `method='linear'`, quote the effective-sample-size correction (applied by default; corrected values quoted), give the slope with its 95% interval and call it significant only if the interval excludes zero.",
        "Trend map: draw the slope at every cell and stipple cells significant at p < 0.05; for the spatial correlation with WOA23 read the coefficient, not its p-value (no spatial correction exists)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "The Atlantic/Indian/Pacific delta SSS values depend on which basin partition is used (here the WOA23 basinmask_01 with marginal seas folded and Southern/Arctic excluded), so the partition must be stated with the numbers.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Basin statistics use the WOA23 basin mask carried onto each grid (`select_basin`, `load_basin_mask`) with `include_marginal_seas=True`; say the mask is a WOA labelling, not the OMIP 10-region one, and that the Southern and Arctic Oceans are separate basins.",
        "Use the surface labels applied through the whole water column (`depth_dependent=False`) for named-ocean means; marginal seas in the WOA23 mask may have no model counterpart, so check the per-basin cell counts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-so-practical-salinity",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-so-practical-salinity.md",
      "sha256": "96f2763290996040d675ca6e8f997ea29fa320b8f6e6793bf2c6fcb739345e19",
      "reason": "SSS must be reported in psu as Practical Salinity regardless of the model's thermodynamics, and TEOS-10 conversions need Absolute Salinity derived from it.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Model `so` (units `0.001`) and WOA23 salinity are both practical-salinity numbers of order 35: difference them directly with no ×0.001/×1000 factor and report in psu; do not pass them as Absolute Salinity into gsw routines."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
