      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are gn (curvilinear native levels) while GFDL-ESM4 is gr (conservatively regridded to 1°×1°), which affects masks, exactness of the comparison and the display regridding for Figure 2.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is `gr`: its \"native\" fields are already remapped to 1° (conserve_order1) with the regridded land–sea mask, so its weights are 1° archive weights; CESM2 (100 km) and MPI (250 km) are `gn` and differ ~2.5× in resolution, so features narrower than the coarse grid are not comparable in amplitude."
      ]
    },
